# Canonical identity per person and per machine.
#
# WHY. Across 60 repositories the estate carries 29 distinct author identities
# for what is a handful of people and a few pieces of automation. Anyone doing
# diligence runs `git shortlog -sne`, sees a scatter of names, and concludes a
# one-person shop with bot noise. That reading is wrong and it is expensive.
#
# A .mailmap fixes it at the reading end. Git applies it to shortlog, log and
# blame, and GitHub honours it in the contributor view. No commit is altered,
# no history is rewritten, nothing needs force-pushing. Drop this in at a repo
# root as `.mailmap` and the same commits read correctly from then on.
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>
# Mapping by commit email alone collapses every display-name spelling that
# address has ever used, which is the whole problem here.

# --- People -----------------------------------------------------------------

# 1402 commits under four spellings: Shayne Heffernan, JackKXCO, KXCO,
# and "Shayne (via Claude)".
Shayne Heffernan <shayne@knightsbridgelaw.com> <shayne@knightsbridgelaw.com>

# 1 commit, an outside contributor. Named so it does not read as staff.
Keral Patel <keralpatel@gmail.com> <keralpatel@gmail.com>

# --- Automation, so it stops being counted as headcount ---------------------

KXCO Automation <ops@kxco.ai> <ops@kxco.ai>
KXCO Automation <ops@kxco.ai> <deploy@kxco.ai>
KXCO Automation <ops@kxco.ai> <builder@local>
KXCO Automation <ops@kxco.ai> <claude-droplet@livetradingnews.com>

# --- UNRESOLVED, deliberately left out ---------------------------------------
#
# These are shared or ambiguous addresses and guessing at them would put the
# wrong name against real work. Resolve each, then add a line here.
#
#   jack@kxco.io                               285 commits
#     One is authored "John Heffernan", the rest "Knightsbridge", "KXCO" and
#     "JackKXCO". If this address is John, one line assigns all 285 to him and
#     it is the single largest correction available.
#
#   hello@kxco.ai                              281 commits
#     Spelled "KXCO", "JackKXCO", "KXCO by Knightsbridge" and, 12 times,
#     "Shayne Heffernan". Looks like a shared org address rather than a person.
#
#   126762857+JackKXCO@users.noreply.github.com  137 commits
#     The GitHub noreply for the JackKXCO account. Whoever holds that account.
#
#   support@knightsbridgelaw.com                96 commits
#     Spelled "Jack KXCO", "JackKXCO" and "One World Builder".
#
#   dev@kxco.io                                 25 commits
#
#   Issaree@knightsbridgelaw.com                 3 commits
#     Authored under the display name "Shayne Heffernan", which is likely a
#     machine with the wrong git config rather than either person.
#
# --- For the people starting now ---------------------------------------------
#
# Mike, Julie and Joe: set this once per machine, before the first commit.
# Merged history does not get rewritten, so an identity set wrongly on day one
# is wrong permanently, and this file can only paper over it afterwards.
#
#   git config --global user.name  "Full Name"
#   git config --global user.email "name@knightsbridgelaw.com"
#
# Then add the matching line above, so the estate reads correctly from the
# first commit rather than after someone notices.
